// main_sync.proto — WHY THE DAEMON COULD NOT BRING A REPOSITORY'S MAIN
// CHECKOUT UP TO ITS UPSTREAM, as it tells the repository's main workspace.
//
// MAIN SYNC IS THE DAEMON'S ALONE. Each sweep of the registered repositories
// fetches every primary branch's upstream and counts the two against each
// other. A branch that is behind and not ahead is fast-forwarded in the main
// checkout (`git merge --ff-only`, never `git pull`, whose behavior follows
// each user's own pull settings), between the main workspace's turns and
// never while the repository's merge queue writes the branch. No workspace is
// involved in a fetch that fails for want of a network: it is logged and
// tried again on the next sweep.
//
// A WORKSPACE IS TOLD ONLY WHAT IT MUST REPAIR. When the fast-forward itself
// fails in the index or the worktree, the daemon submits a MainSyncFailure to
// the repository's main workspace as a deferred prompt of origin
// conversation.v1.PromptOrigin.PROMPT_ORIGIN_MAIN_SYNC_REPAIR, asking it to
// bring the branch to the upstream tip; a closed main workspace is reopened
// to receive it. One failure is told once per upstream commit and cause: the
// same failure found by the next sweep is logged, not told again, and a newer
// upstream commit supersedes an untold notice.

